data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_part.done","sequence_number":98,"item_id":"rs_097f9471457aa523016ac9e1b4c1208196aa8adb31219bbe25","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"part":{"type":"summary_text","text":"**Considering test migrations**\n\nI'm thinking about whether I need to add an import for the SQLite seed into my project. The existing tests start from an empty state, so maybe I should create a separate migration test to see if the schema needs to be populated first. If the original schema works with the migration, that could be enough. Also, I wonder if I really need a separate test since using an empty schema with existing counts might suffice. I'll keep this in mind as I move forward."}}

